$checks = CheckboxList( [ '\(x<m\)', '\(x>m\)', '\(x=m\)', 'all real \(x\)' ], [ '\(x<m\)' ], labels => "ABC", displayLabels => 1 );
############################################################ # Body ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML Let [`g(x)=\frac{1}{s\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{(x-m)^2}{2s^2}}\text{,}`] where [`s>0\text{.}`] Find the range of [`x`] values for which [`g'(x)`] is positive.
[_]{$checks}{5}
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION The constant factor [`\frac{1}{s\sqrt{2\pi}}`] is positive. Differentiating the exponential part gives
[``` \begin{aligned} g'(x) &= \frac{1}{s\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{(x-m)^2}{2s^2}} \left(-\frac{x-m}{s^2}\right). \end{aligned} ```]
The exponential factor is always positive, so the sign of [`g'(x)`] is determined by [`-(x-m)\text{.}`] Therefore, [`g'(x)>0`] when [`x<m\text{.}`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
